 "text": "Every morning, Anna takes the 7:45 train to the city. It's not a long trip — about twenty-five minutes — but she doesn't waste it. She reads.\n\nLast year she finished 32 books. \"Some were easy, some weren't,\" she says with a smile. Her favourite was a short novel about a lighthouse keeper who lived alone on a rock in the North Sea for 1,200 days.\n\nWhy read on a train? \"Because nobody can call me there,\" Anna laughs. \"Well, they can. I just don't answer.\" She thinks that reading in English every day, even for ten minutes, has helped her more than any course she's ever paid for.\n",
